STRUCTURAL DAMAGE DESCRIPTORS

For each disturbance:

MAGNITUDE

fraction of members whose:
functional-region relation
changes.

SPATIAL CONCENTRATION

how many accepted regions contain:
most of the affected members.

DIFFUSION

normalized entropy of:
affected-member mass
across:
accepted regions.

VALUE MASS

fraction of current active-value mass
inside:
the affected set.

BOUNDARY MASS

fraction of challenged relations
that cross:
accepted region boundaries.

These are:
observable estimates

derived from:
relational contradiction / quarantine evidence.

Policies do not receive:
the true damage labels.

STRUCTURAL REPAIR DEBT

Primary trust-region controller tracks:

D =
0.30 * cumulative_membership_displacement
+
0.20 * quarantined_fraction
+
0.15 * relational_disagreement
+
0.15 * affected_value_mass
+
0.10 * normalized_damage_diffusion
+
0.10 * failed_patch_pressure.

All terms:
normalized to [0,1].

CUMULATIVE MEMBERSHIP DISPLACEMENT

Fraction of members whose:
accepted region identity

has changed
since:
the last globally validated topology.

This debt is:
cumulative.

Ten:
1% patches

can therefore become:
a 10% structural displacement

even if:
each individual patch
was small.

FAILED PATCH PRESSURE

0:
no failed bounded repair.

0.5:
one repeated unsuccessful patch cycle.

1:
three or more consecutive failed cycles.

PRIMARY TRUST REGION

Incremental patching remains admissible only while:

D <= 0.25

AND

quarantine fraction <=25%

AND

normalized damage diffusion <=0.45

AND

no single accepted patch
moves:
>8% of family membership

AND

failed patch cycles <3.

Crossing ANY hard boundary:

closes:
the repair trust region.

TRUST-REGION EXIT

When:
the repair region closes,

TRUST-REGION + BLASTEMA policy:

- freezes broad action
  only for:
  affected / uncertified scope;

- preserves:
  unaffected vested certificates;

- launches:
  H144 de-novo candidate redevelopment;

- validates:
  the new topology
  on:
  fresh evidence;

- reuses:
  H146 certificates
  only where:
  their region / boundary assumptions
  still hold.

This differs from:
full-family epistemic amnesia.

CERTIFICATE INHERITANCE RULE

A vested certificate may survive:
an accepted bounded patch

only when:

1. member region identity is unchanged;
2. member's local boundary class is unchanged;
3. topology epoch for that unaffected region is unchanged;
4. no contradiction debt threshold has been crossed.

Affected members:

certificate ->
CHALLENGED / INVALID.

Unaffected regions:

retain:
valid dormant certificates.

SPLIT INHERITANCE

When one region splits:

members inside:
the split parent

lose:
region-boundary validity.

Other regions:

retain certificates.

MERGE INHERITANCE

When two regions merge:

members in:
both merged parents

require:
new region certificate.

Other regions:
retain.

BLASTEMA INHERITANCE

After de-novo redevelopment:

certificate reuse is allowed only for:

members whose:
pre- and post-redevelopment
local relational neighborhood

remains:
equivalent under:
fresh validation.

Otherwise:
invalidate.

